<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Alta River (1068)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1068">1068</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Alta River was fought in 1068 near Pereyaslavl, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumans">Cumans</a> (Polovtsians) defeated the combined forces of three sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-the-wise">Yaroslav the Wise</a>: Iziaslav of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-i-of-kiev">Sviatoslav</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a> and Vsevolod of Pereyaslavl. It was the first major Cuman victory over the Rus', and it led to an uprising in Kyiv that briefly drove out Iziaslav.</p></div>
